<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" style="background: #f0f0f0; margin: 0; padding: 0;">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <title>Preview</title>
  <style>
    *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
  </style>
</head>
<%# ⚠️ DO NOT SIMPLIFY - Body IS the A4 page (2026-03-01)
    ════════════════════════════════════════════
    Why: Template content includes inline <style> blocks (266+ lines).
    When wrapped in a <div>, the browser's HTML parser (in iframe srcDoc)
    restructures the DOM — the wrapper div gets "closed" and all styled
    content falls OUTSIDE it, appearing on the grey body background.
    ❌ WRONG: <div class="a4-page"><%= yield_content %></div>
    ✅ CORRECT: <body> itself is styled as the A4 page — no wrapper div.
    The <style> block is valid directly inside <body> and won't break parsing.
    ════════════════════════════════════════════ -%>
<body style="width: 210mm; min-height: 297mm; padding: 15mm 18mm; margin: 10px auto; background: white; border: 1px solid #000; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">
  <%= yield_content %>
</body>
</html>
